npm init -y => y hamaray lia nodejs application ko initiate karti ha

npm i express => it installs express package

const app = express() => this line create an instance of a server and we save it in app

app.listen(3000) => y server ko start karnay ka lia use hoti ha aur 3000 is port number

example : in laptop there are multiple applications like mail, files etc so mail use port 25 and email use port 20 , so same like this server needs 3000 port number

(req, res) => req is => jo data frontend sa ata ha us ko sirf req sa access kar sakty ho
res => kuch bi data ko backend sa frontend ko bajna ho to res use karty ha

API : application programming interface : do alag alag applications ko communicate karwany ka lia jo set of rules and protocols hum use karty ha usko hum api kahty ha
e.g frontend and backend these two may be separate application

REST API: this is type of api and is most common type of web api , is ka kuch rules ha like agar ap ko 2 applications ko communicate karwana ha to wo sab say pehly standart protocol ko use kary gi like HTTP , GET, POST, PUT, DELETE are most common methods

HTTP Methods: GET, POST PUT, PATCH, DELETE
GET => server sa data mangwana ho
POST => sever per data send karna ho
PATCH => data already present ha aur us data ko update karna ho
DELETE => server per data ha aur usy delete karna ha